    "explanation": "ECONOMIC RATIONALE FOR M3 vs M5 CONVERGENCE AT MONTH 96 AND DIVERGENCE AT MONTH 360:\n1. Pre-Milestone H (Months 1 to 96): Both M3 and M5 share identical inflows (Scenario C: 500 + 0.50*delta_Y) and identical state machine rules. Vaso 4 Core-Satellite allocation requires crossing a 100,000 EUR threshold before Satellite ETF allocation is unlocked. At Month 96, Vaso 4 has received only 40% of flows for ~45 months, reaching ~12,000 EUR, well below 100,000 EUR. Thus, in both M3 and M5, 100% of Vaso 4 flows go to Core ETF, meaning zero Satellite assets exist and zero rebalancing is triggered prior to Month 96. Consequently, all pots (V1, V2, V3b, V3a, V4) are 100% identical trajectory-by-trajectory at Month 96, explaining why PGF (100.00%), UGF (95.26%), UGapF (0.22%), and CVaR (1293.85 EUR) are mathematically identical.\n2. Maximum Drawdown (MDD): In S-DFP, Market MDD is Time-Weighted Return (TWR) of invested assets. Total Wealth MDD reflects the Milestone H car purchase at Month 96. Because financial wealth up to Month 96 is identical, the 95th percentile of MDD is identical (63.47%).\n3. Post-Milestone H (Months 97 to 360): Vaso 4 crosses 100,000 EUR around Year 16-18. From that point onward, M3 rebalances via annual asset sales incurring capital gains tax drag (1099 EUR), whereas M5 uses pure Inflow Rebalancing within tolerance band [0.35, 0.45], reducing tax drag to 616 EUR. The compounded friction savings create the +884 EUR marginal median wealth advantage of M5 (+587 EUR paired differences median; HL pseudomedian: +776 EUR)."
  },
  "point_2_w_total_available_h_definition": {
    "Regulatory_Framework": "D.Lgs. 252/2005 (Disciplina delle forme pensionistiche complementari)",
    "Legal_Constraint": "Vaso 0 (TFR / Fondo Pensione) cannot be liquidated for car purchases or general consumer goals under Italian law. It is strictly excluded from available funds at Milestone H.",
    "S_DFP_Definition": "W_total_available_H = V_3a(H) + V_3a_cash(H) + max(0, V_1(H) - 500) + V_2(H) + V_4_core(H) + V_4_sat(H)",
    "Vaso_3b_Treatment": "Vaso 3b (Mortgage safety reserve of 4 installments) serves as an operational hard-floor and is protected from car purchase liquidation.",
    "Fair_Benchmark_Definition": "W_total_available_H = max(0, Cash_buffer(H) - 500) + Equity_portfolio(H) + Bond_portfolio(H) (excluding Vaso 0)",
    "Naive_Benchmark_Definition": "W_total_available_H = Equity_portfolio(H) + Bond_portfolio(H) (excluding Vaso 0)"
  },
